          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6233b8f00a30b5facc81852cf0e2b80047798f684e7a5bb58ded1d29a518b3dc:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_45c05a9a4c184693998ae9431ad2ba03",
      "statement": "The JWKS resolver is created with jose's createRemoteJWKSet and cached in a module-level Map keyed by JWKS URL for the entire process lifetime — mota never evicts or recreates it and passes jose no caching options, so re-fetching is governed by jose defaults (5s fetch timeout, 30s cooldown, 10min cache age) with an immediate re-fetch for an unknown kid outside cooldown, which is what makes Supabase key rotation work without a mota restart.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://apps/api/src/auth/supabaseJwt.ts#L14-L29",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ae77ac5a3c349c46e45f526415d66a0f893bfdb8ff6777d21922a8c821caef96:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_28f53396815d4944b14f3dad354fe097",
      "statement": "Inside verifyAccessToken, any thrown error whose string code starts with ERR_ (every jose JOSEError subclass — expired, bad signature, claim validation failed, no matching key, JWKS timeout, etc.) is classified as an invalid token and returns null, not an outage; only errors outside jose's taxonomy, such as a Node network error from the JWKS fetch, are re-thrown as SupabaseUnavailableError.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://apps/api/src/auth/supabaseJwt.ts#L16-L19",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:281294427a3236276a76c3f30bb8cbd87df5ea29407625605ffd1bc75e6b3834:"
        },
        {
