      "statement": "fake-supabase's signAccessToken mints tokens with the correct issuer (`${url}/auth/v1`), audience 'authenticated', role 'authenticated', and a configurable sub, email, and expiresIn (negative values produce already-expired tokens), which is how the suites exercise real JWT semantics — garbage tokens resolve to null, expired tokens resolve to anonymous — instead of mocking the verifier.",
