    {
      "id": "claim_0526460757a44de28c0223b92d678a42",
      "statement": "The e2e suite pins the product decision that an upstream outage must not be reported as an anonymous user: with an oauthConfig whose fetcher always throws, a request carrying a refresh cookie returns 503 AUTH_UPSTREAM_UNAVAILABLE rather than 200 authenticated:false, because silently degrading an authenticated user risks overwriting their server settings with local ones.",
